 "discussions": [
  {
   "id": "d_m9",
   "title": "Discussion: Was There a Better Way to End the War With Japan?",
   "html": "<div id=\"sparkled-assessment\"><div style=\"background:#2D1B1F; border-bottom:4px solid #8F2433; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:20px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px; color:#F3B9C2; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>DISCUSSION</strong></div><div style=\"font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:26px; color:#FFFFFF; line-height:1.25; margin-bottom:6px;\">Discussion: Was There a Better Way to End the War With Japan?</div><div style=\"font-size:15px; color:#F6E1E4;\">10 points · threaded discussion</div></div><div style=\"border-top:3px double #8F2433; margin:0 0 20px;\"></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #3F6B2F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#3F6B2F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you start</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Open the lessons \"The Arsenal at Home\" and \"Okinawa, the Bomb, and the Surrender\". Use My Notebook on those pages to gather your notes and marks, then come back here to post.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2D1B1F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2D1B1F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>The question</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">In August 1945, American leaders used two atomic bombs to end the war with Japan. Was there a better way? Possible alternatives included an invasion, a longer blockade, a demonstration of the weapon, a clearer promise about the emperor, or waiting for the Soviet attack. Your job is to decide whether one of these would have been better than what was done, or whether the choice made was the best one available at the time.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #8F2433; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#8F2433; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your post (about 100 to 150 words):</strong></p><ol style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 6px; padding-left:22px;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Take a clear position: a better way existed, none did, or it is too hard to know.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Give one specific piece of evidence from the source Korematsu v. United States or Truman's statement that supports you.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Name one fact that cuts against your position, and explain why you still hold it.</li></ol></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #3F6B2F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#3F6B2F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your reply</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your reply (about 50 to 75 words):</strong> Respond to one classmate. Do you agree with their reasoning? If so, strengthen it with something they did not use. If not, say respectfully where their reasoning falls short.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2D1B1F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2D1B1F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Post first, then reply. You will not see your classmates' posts until you have posted. Remember that the leaders of 1945 did not know how things would turn out. Judge their choices by what they knew then, and say so when you are using what we know now.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #2D1B1F; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#2D1B1F; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Rubric</strong></div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin-top:6px;\"><tbody><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#F6E1E4; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Post and reply<br><span style=\"color:#8F2433;\">10.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>10.0 pts</strong> Substantive<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Clear position, specific evidence from the week, names a counterpoint, and the reply engages a classmate's actual reasoning</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>6.0 pts</strong> Thin<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Position stated but evidence vague, no counterpoint, or the reply only says \"I agree\"</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> Missing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">No post, or no reply</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",
